Regardless of the vaccine status, all guests over the age of 2 must arrive at the cruise terminal 3 nights or more before boarding and have a negative Covid-19 test.
But if you test it too early, it won’t count. The logistics of when and where to conduct the test before your cruise is a bit confusing, so this is the information you need to know about the Covid-19 test before you cruise so that you can board the plane without any problems.
Basically, Royal Caribbean stated that the day you set sail was not one of the days you calculated. Instead, count down from the day before to determine which day to test.
Depending on where you live, there are different options for testing. This includes free or additional test sites.
Some federal programs for people who do not have insurance. Another option is Passport Health, which has more than 100 locations across the country and caters to people who are traveling or returning to school.
You might even find some test sites that offer drive-through testing, where you don’t need to leave the car. Roll down the car window, wipe it clean, and hit the road.
There are very few guarantees as to when you will get results, but testing earlier in the time window before your cruise ship’s departure is the safest option.
You can choose to print it out or use a digital copy. Royal Caribbean recommends printing results whenever possible to simplify the process of displaying results.
