To celebrate Mid-Autumn Festival, Baron organized a special Bo Bing event for all the employees of Overseas Department.
So we went to a delicate restaurant and had a wonderful dinner together. It was certainly a delightful Mid-Autumn celebration with special event and delicious food, endless conversations, and most importantly, the bonds formed tighter among us.
The Mid-Autumn Festival, also known as Moon Festival or Mooncake Festival(literally translated from Zhong-qiu-jie), is a traditional festival loved by Chinese people and the second-most important holiday after the Chinese New Year. The festival is an important harvest celebration which is held on the 15th day of the 8th month of the Chinese lunar calendar with a full moon at night.
Bo Bing is a Chinese dice game traditionally played as part of the celebration of the Mid-Autumn Festival. In modern times, the game has 63 different price of gifts as prizes for the winning players, including daily necessities, household appliances or money.
Needless to say, today’s Mid-Autumn Festival is a holiday for family reunion. Contact
