Do you know why baby has diaper rashes?
Diaper rashes grow in warm and moist places, particularly in your baby’s diaper. You baby’s skin will become sore, red and tender if she/he has diaper rashes.
·spots or blisters in the diaper area
·Bacteria or yeast. The area covered by a diaper- buttocks, thighs and genitals- is especially vulnerable because it’s warm and moist, making it a perfect breeding ground for bacteria and yeast.
·Change diaper frequently. Remember not to expose your baby’s bottom area prolongedly to wet or dirty diapers.
Rinse your baby’s bottom with warm water during each diaper change. Consider using a barrier ointment after rinsing the baby’s bottom to prevent skin irritation.
·Avoid irritants. Use baby wipes and breathable diapers which do not contain alcohol, fragrance or other harmful chemicals.
