Have you ever heard of diatomaceous earth, also known as DE?
The uses for diatomaceous earth in the garden are great. Diatomaceous earth is a truly amazing all-natural product that can help you grow a beautiful and healthy garden.
Diatomaceous earth is made from fossilized water plants and is a naturally occurring siliceous sedimentary mineral compound from the remains of algae-like plants called diatoms. The plants have been part of Earth’s ecology system dating back to prehistoric times.
One of the benefits of diatomaceous earth for insect control is that the insects have no way to build up a resistance to it, which can’t be said for many chemical control insecticides.
The directions will include how to properly apply the diatomaceous earth (DE) both in the garden and indoors for the control of many insects as well as forming a barrier of sorts against them.
