News - Against the trend to break through and overcome difficulties, why does China’s economy “not drop the chain”
Against the trend to break through and overcome difficulties, why does China’s economy “not drop the chain”
In one month, the daily output of masks has increased by more than ten times, and the rapid operation of the supply chain is an important basis for winning the battle against epidemic prevention and control; offline influence, cloud compensation, hindered foreign trade, expansion of domestic sales, and flexible changes of enterprises Behind the “body” is the efficient coordination of the industrial chain. The economic system is interlocking.
As the end of the year is approaching, a reporter from Xinhua News Agency will join you to see how China’s economy “will not drop the link” at critical moments this year.
In 7 days, I drove more than 1,000 kilometers from north to south, and I visited filter manufacturers one after another. Recalling the hardships at the beginning of the year, Cao Jun, chairman of the mask manufacturer Lanhe Medical, is still vividly remembered.
With industry reputation, timely visits and expansion of meltblown cloth production capacity, Lanhe finally overcome the difficulties. “Since then, we have signed long-term agreements with many partners to diversify risks as much as possible.”
In 2020, the three words supply chain will have a very different weight to China’s economy.
200,000 mainstream computer models, each motherboard requires thousands of components. When materials are in short supply, what kind of order matching will bring maximum benefit?
Guan Wei, senior vice president of Lenovo’s global supply chain, told reporters that beginning in the first half of the year, Lenovo has developed models based on multi-dimensional indicators such as efficiency, market, and scale, and achieved the most effective output with limited supply. Through smart upgrades, computer turnover can increase by 5% in a quarter.
At the worst, I even thought that production and sales would drop by 25%.” Ye Shengji, deputy secretary-general of the China Association of Automobile Manufacturers, said that the joint efforts of the state, various departments and enterprises have allowed the supply chain to recover quickly. The industry is picking up month by month, “the entire production and sales will be close to last year’s level.”
Grasp the opportunity in the “chain”
Joining the ranks of “Double 11″, Fang Hao, the manufacturer of sticky wool and the person in charge of Zhejiang Yiwu Zexi Daily Necessities Co., Ltd., “returned the game.” He was the main exporter and lost 10 million yuan in orders due to the epidemic at the beginning of the year. Through the flexible supply chain, it was transferred to domestic sales.
One-key unlocking, the electric vehicle will come intelligently; parking sensor, after use, the vehicle will automatically drive to the return point… Based on the complete ecological chain of data, sensing, etc., No. 9 Company has launched a new intelligent electric vehicle and short-term transportation plan to achieve the right Full-cycle deployment management of vehicles.
“In the future, the competition of enterprises will evolve into the collaborative competition of the industrial ecology in which they are located.” said Liu Duo, president of the China Academy of Information and Communications Technology. Consolidate the foundation under the “chain”
Some leading companies are also playing a good “first move” in the new development pattern.
The Ministry of Industry and Information Technology comprehensively sorted out the list of leading enterprises and core supporting enterprises in key areas; eight departments launched pilot projects for innovative applications of supply chains…accelerating the transformation of supply chains to supply networks, and a series of measures were launched accordingly.
“We will introduce more specific measures to strengthen the industrial foundation and upgrade the modernization level of the industrial chain, to promote the accumulation of more innovative elements, and to serve high-quality development.” said Huang Libin, a spokesperson for the Ministry of Industry and Information Technology.
