News - Mid-Year Economic Observation|Under the pressure and challenge, how can Chinese manufacturing break through?
Mid-Year Economic Observation|Under the pressure and challenge, how can Chinese manufacturing break through?
The international epidemic continues to spread, and the global economy is in a downturn; downward pressure on the domestic economy is increasing, and the pace of structural adjustment is deepening. 2020 is not unusual for Chinese manufacturing.
The reporter went to many places to investigate and found that proactive response and proactive change is a true portrayal of many manufacturing companies. In the process of responding to challenges, Made in China continued to lay a solid foundation, sought opportunities in crisis, and made the pace of transition to high quality more steadily.
“Some of the orders in the process were’halted halfway,’ and some scattered orders were directly invalidated.” Risk challenges made Yang Hua, chairman of Wish Wish Home Textile Co., Ltd., once “very anxious.” Founded 22 years ago, Wish Home Textiles has been OEM for many international brands, and has experienced great storms and waves, but this year has encountered an unprecedented crisis. Self-help is imminent, and Yang Hua is determined to reform the process and turn exports to domestic sales.
Figure… In June, China’s manufacturing purchasing managers’ index rose by 0.3 percentage points from the previous month; the production index and the new order index rose by 0.7 and 0.5 percentage points from the previous month; the profits of industrial enterprises in May increased by 6% year-on-year…a series of data confirms The manufacturing industry is recovering steadily.
The challenge is big, and there are more opportunities in it
The force of the epidemic and the pressure of survival have made many traditional industries realize that intelligence is the top priority related to the way of survival and the quality of development. Efforts to seize digital opportunities are the active choice of many companies.
Lianbao Technology CEO Bai Peng said that with the help of digitalization, the company’s cumulative shipments have increased significantly. The next step is to extend intelligent management to the entire industrial chain.
“Artificial intelligence has initially proved its potential to disrupt and restructure the industry.” Baidu Chairman Li Yanhong said, “new infrastructure” will promote the application of artificial intelligence in transportation, energy and other fields, greatly improve efficiency, and drive economic development.
While the decline in manufacturing investment has narrowed, investment in high-tech manufacturing from January to May increased by 2.7% year-on-year. Behind the numbers is the market’s recovery and innovation.
“We give priority to paying hundreds of millions of yuan to supporting enterprises, and we will increase local supporting facilities while doing a good job of resuming work in coordination,” said Lu Wenjun, deputy general manager of China First Heavy Industry Group Co., Ltd. The proportion of local supporting facilities has increased from less than 20% to 52%.
The Ministry of Industry and Information Technology has comprehensively sorted out the list of leading enterprises and core supporting enterprises in key areas; eight departments launched pilot projects for innovative applications in the supply chain; increased support for small and medium-sized enterprises…a series of measures were launched accordingly.
