Top 5 Things-To-Know Before Buying Your Digital Weight Scale
We already know that when you start eating healthier and exercising, then getting healthier is quicker and longer sustained if your are also monitoring your weight and health factors closely.
Choosing the right digital bathroom scale is not quite that easy though.
Some have extra features so you can be monitoring more than just your body weight.
For Most People, The Choice Is Clear Between Digital and Analog
These analog scales, however, are actually becoming almost obsolete these days.
The analog models don’t have as wide a range for measurement, or the capabilities (and often accuracy) that their digital competitors have.
Do you want to just look at your weight?
Are you worried about your overall health?
Another thing to think about is the number of people who are going to be using the body weight scale and their individual concerns.
All these factors will determine the type of scale you’ll need.
One thing is for sure, the things you can expect from a scale these days go way beyond your old 90s bathroom set.
You can now program your age, height, gender, and activity level in your scale and it can estimate your metabolic age and even advise you on calorie intake.
In essence, scales today go far beyond measuring just your BMI, to establish your health.
You might like to measure daily, or even take a measurement pre and post work-out – so accuracy and reliability is key.
But, if you’re a professional athlete or a body builder and you regularly measure your body fat and muscle weight by visiting health centres, then the at home scale accuracy might be an issue.
However, you’d be surprised because an increase in price spent on a set of scales does not always show an increase in accuracy.
Added features can dramatically increase the price of your scale.
They could just be the best digital bathroom scale for you.
Many of us leave our scales out for easy measurements and our visitors to see, our scale can be ‘furniture’ in your bathroom.
If you have poor eyesight, the digital bathroom scale that talks to you could be scales for you.
Many of the talking scales now have different language options available such as Spanish, French, and most other European languages.
Remember that some types of body weight scales that can keep a journal of your weight, also can show you what the recorded weight was after you get off the scale so you can have a closer look.
Personally, we’re surprised Withings can find people to buy their scale with a price tag of over $1000, but.. you know, to each their own.
