What do you have to do to marry in Denmark?
Please pay 250 Euro to the account specified by us so that we can transfer the fee to the Danish authorities and start processing immediately. The processing can only begin when all documents are available, the amount has been received by us and the forms have been filled in correctly and signed.
We also help you with contacts to florists, hotels, apartments, restaurants, hairdressers etc. In some cases, you must be present at 1 the day before the wedding at the registry office and in other cases, everything can be done in one day, with no accommodation requirement or performance date.
Saturday dates are also possible with us, and 2 witnesses can be provided on request.
Everything worked perfectly and the officials have given us a very good time. The wedding was held in an old town hall and it was very romantic.
We had big problems marrying in Germany and are so happy that it was possible in Denmark. We had a wonderful marriage in the registry office on an island.
Please note that our prices are staggered and depend on whether you are single or divorced / widowed. The prices are therefore shown PER PERSON.
119 Euro for DHL shipping (courier mail), if the letter should be sent outside the EU, or in very urgent cases.
595 Euro for express legalization within 1-2 weeks
EXTRA CHARGE of 550 Euro / couple for a marriage outside the registry office, eg on the beach, in the lighthouse, hotel or garden. The fees from the registry office are included in the price.
EXTRA CHARGE of 350 euros for a sworn interpreter during the wedding in Denmark. special wishes
