China is the largest producer of rare earth minerals, accounting for 62.9% of the total rare earth mineral products in 2019, followed by the United States and Australia, accounting for 12.4% and 10% respectively. Thanks to rare earth reserves, China has become the world’s largest production base and export base of rare earth magnets.
