With the development of downstream applications, the output of NdFeB magnet materials in China has been growing rapidly. According to the data of China Rare Earth Industry Association in 2019, the output of sintered Neodymium blanks was 170000 tons, accounting for 94.3% of the total output of Neodymium magnetic materials in that year, bonded NdFeB accounted for 4.4%, and other total output accounted for only 1.3%.
Global downstream consumption of NdFeB is distributed in the motor industry, bus and railway, intelligent robot, wind power generation and new energy vehicles. The growth rate of the above industries in the next five years will all exceed 10%, which will lead to the increase of Neodymium production in China.
