MetaMask is the wallet (wallet) by default of most Ethereum-based DeFi applications and has more than five million monthly active users. In addition to offering a wallet service, MetaMask also provides swaps that allow users to exchange tokens from the wallet.
MetaMask works as an extension for the Chrome and Firefox browsers. It allows users to store data related to Ethereum, such as public addresses and private keys, like any other Ethereum wallet (that is, you can save your tokens there), and it allows users to interact with websites that run Ethereum-based applications and smart contracts (that is, it turns your web browser into an Ethereum browser).
The bottom line is that MetaMask allows users to do anything Ethereum-related (like interact with smart contracts, send / store / receive Ether, or interact with Ethereum-based web applications) simply by running a browser extension.
A default account will be created with an associated Ethereum public address on the Main Network. You can use that account, or you can add accounts by clicking the circular looking button in the upper right corner of MetaMask.
Log into your Binance or Coinbase account and send Ether or BNB (for example) to an address associated with an account created in MetaMask. To get your public address that was created automatically when you created your MetaMask vault, click the "..." icon and click "copy address to clipboard".
This works like it would on any other website, click the product, click the buy now button, confirm the transaction. The only note is that your final confirmation will be in MetaMask (you will see a screen that confirms details such as fees), now wait.
