Relai is a Swiss investment app in bitcoins that you can use to buy and sell bitcoins anonymously, supplying only the number of your bank account. To use Relai, you do not need to register an account or send personal documents such as ID or passport.
In Relai you can buy Bitcoin without KYC (Know Your Customer stands for Know your customer). That is, you do not need to provide your personal data or open an account.
There is no registration and therefore no tedious verification process.
It only supports a single payment method: bank transfer.
Open the app and select Buy BTC
Enter the number of times you want to buy bitcoin. You can select once, weekly or monthly
In addition, when making the payment, copy the payment message that has been shown in the application. Once you have made the payment, you will receive the bitcoin
Enter the amount you want to sell.
Enter the IBAN number and your name.
Verify and copy your new Bitcoin address into the Relai wallet when you want to make the transfer.
Relai is compatible with all European countries, such as Germany, Austria, Denmark, Sweden, the Netherlands, Italy, Poland, Spain, Belgium and France. Unfortunately, you cannot use their service if your bank uses the Know Your Customer (KYC) requirements and is registered in the following countries: Ireland, Ukraine, Cyprus, Monaco, Kosovo, Malta, Belarus, Russia, Bosnia and Herzegovina or Faroe Islands.
Due to money laundering regulations and fraud detection systems, Relai imposes transaction limits for both buying and selling bitcoin:
There are other fees that are charged on Bitcoin networks.
UK customers can also use these services if their banks offer a Euro account. UK citizens can easily set up a euro account if they have a free bank account from providers like Revolut and Wise, formerly Transferwise.
Relai is a non-custodial wallet, which means they don't hold funds or bitcoin. They use private keys that are encrypted on your mobile phone to secure customer assets.
