There are hours until the Ethereum update that threatens to change the operation of transaction fees forever and that, in addition, will begin to destroy coins.
There are hours until the Ethereum update that threatens to change the way transaction fees work forever and that, in addition, it will begin to destroy coins. Although the so-called Ethereum 1559 update was scheduled for August 4, it has been slightly delayed and will finally come out tomorrow Thursday.
3 It will destroy the coins and could power the ether
With this Ethereum update, transaction fees will be more predictable
EIP-1559 has excited the crypto community because it will destroy or burn ether, the cryptocurrency of the Ethereum network. Now, miners will not receive the base quota to avoid the possibility of artificially congesting the network to keep the quota high.
But the influence on price is far from certain, say the developers. It also depends on factors such as transaction volumes, which determine the magnitude of gas rates and thus the amount of ether that is destroyed.
After the Ethereum upgrade, transaction fees don't have to be cheaper
In Ethereum 2.0, the network will move from a "proof of work" system to a "proof of stake" system (Proof of work y proof of stake). In the proof-of-work system, miners use large amounts of computing power to verify transactions.
You can read the official notes on this Ethereum update in its official website.
