Although Cardano and Ethereum have several zeros of difference in their prices, no one has any doubt that the so-called Ethereum Killer is very serious. The next few months promise to be very exciting in the crypto and smart contract ecosystem.
For this implementation, dcSpark claims to have developed a novel technology called "Wrapped smart contracts." This feature allows teams to deploy EVM-compliant smart contracts on the sidechain without having to move Cardano's native smart contracts to the sidechain.
For this reason, many competing Layer 1 networks have struggled to offer some kind of interoperability with Ethereum, with the help of sidechains or independent networks.
In the past, the team has faced criticism for slow launches and a lack of smart contracts. In recent months, Cardano has made significant progress and gradually resolved the implementation schedule for smart contracts.
We tell you what is behind Cardano, one of the strongest future bets in the crypto world and a rival to take into account to perhaps dethrone Bitcoin and Ethereum in the future, especially in the field of energy consumption, the decentralized finance and smart contracts.
The name of the project honors the illustrious mathematician Girolamo Cardano, known for early systemic probability calculations. Cardano's cryptocurrency is Ada, named after Ada Lovelace who is considered the first computer programmer.
Cardano is an open source blockchain, as well as a platform designed to execute smart contracts (once the arrival of the third phase of the roadmap de Cardano where smart contracts are contemplated).
Cardano is similar in some respects to Ethereum, but without much of the bloat associated with the latter. This allows Cardano to scale to meet the growing demands of the cryptocurrency, without compromising speed or efficiency.
Ada also partnered with the Nigerian government to be able to provide health-related education, to those who cannot afford basic medical care, while rewarded with cryptocurrencies that will allow them to pay for doctors and medicines while learning, through the Ask The Doctor application.
All the technologies used in Cardano have gone through a long period of development, scientific and peer review around the world, something that Bitcoin, Ethereum and many other cryptos have overlooked.
A slot leader is chosen for each time slot and is held responsible for adding a block to the chain. To guard against attempts to subvert the protocol, each new slot leader must consider the last blocks of the chain received as transients: only the chain that precedes a pre-specified number of transient blocks is considered resolved.
This would allow Cardano to apply additional consensus rules on top of this layer, allowing it to join and interoperate with other networks.
Cardano's next step is to include smart contracts in your network, what will happen with the arrival of the Goguen phase. With this update, Cardano will have the ability to maintain DApps on its network which will be programmed using the Plutus programming language, an adaptation of Haskell for this blockchain.
The main objective of this update is interoperability and the inclusion of sidechains, which will allow Cardano to offer its services in a much more optimized way and with at least two orders of magnitude in its capabilities.
Cardano's last stage is to achieve governance on-chain and with it, a greater decentralization than that achieved with Shelley, as well as achieving self-sufficiency in its development. To do this, Voltaire will create a governance infrastructure on-chain and a decentralized treasury system, in order to maintain financing for the project and its healthy development over time.
