An ETF is an investment fund whose shares are traded and settled in exactly the same way as shares. There are not a few beginners who do not know how to buy Bitcoin.
Douglas Yones, director of publicly traded products at the NYSE, also addressed the momentous occasion, but suggested that there is still progress on cryptocurrency investment products. "This is an exciting step, but not the last," he told The New York Times.
A rocky road to approval
In general, you are concerned about the volatility of cryptocurrency prices and the potential for price manipulation in the largely unregulated Bitcoin ecosystem. Major cryptocurrency exchanges, which are used to set spot prices for bitcoin exchange-traded products, are not registered with the SEC, making it difficult for the agency to verify their trading flow.
They do not involve owning actual bitcoin or negotiating spot prices. Instead, the CME calculates a Bitcoin benchmark rate (BRR) over a one-hour window based on the trading flow of major spot exchanges.
Still, the debut of a futures-based Bitcoin ETF is cause for celebration. It represents a significant evolution in the move towards a fund based on bitcoin spot prices.
