How to read cryptocurrency charts is an art available to everyone. Don't be fooled by the apparent complexity of the world of cryptocurrency, FOREX or Bitcoin chart analysis: learning to interpret price charts is easy.
5.1 How to read cryptocurrency charts: head and shoulders pattern
While alltraders They use graphics, not all uses are the same. Especially in the trading world: a Warren Buffett-style stock investor, much more interested in the fundamental analysis, you will only use a chart to measure market sentiment, that is, does the market like or dislike this action?
Bullish- An uptrend means that the price is rising.
Side: a lateral trend, in which the price neither rises nor falls significantly, but moves laterally.
With line charts we cannot answer questions like "How wide is the daily trading range?"
Most candlestick charts are based on a daily time period, which means that each candle represents one day of trading activity. trading.
Opening- The first price the crypto traded at when the candle opened (this varies depending on the candle time frame we are using).
Remember: the open, high, low and close depend on the time frame of the chart. For example, a five minute chart has a new open every five minutes, each time a new candle is created.
Bullish candlesticks: when the closing price is above the opening price. On most charting platforms, bullish candles are either green or white.
The analysis of the changes between these candle elements is the backbone of the analysis of many traders /operators. This style can be called «Trade of Price Action ', with Steve Nison and Al Brooks being famous advocates.
All traders successful are, at heart, full-time professionals in the economic branch of thebehavioral finance, a branch of economics based on the study of human behavior and all the variables that determine our decision-making process. Price charts are nothing more than the most efficient way to capture irrational market behavior in real time.
They refer to the number of shares or crypto trades traded in a given period; In this example, each bar represents one day of trading activity (daily chart). Volume is useless on an individual basis: you always need to check the volume along with the price.
So far we have been talking about daily charts, but the truth is that stock charts can be used for any period of time: from monthly charts to ten-second charts.
The amount of risk you want to take on each trade.
All values fluctuate and, for there to be growth, there must be decrease. The most prominent method to quantify volatility in a given period of time is through the Average True Range Indicator.
While we are not going to devote too much space in this article to individual candlestick analysis, we are going to take a look at two of these critical candlesticks to get a better idea of some of the fundamentals of technical analysis carried out by chartists most passionate about studying candlesticks. .
The stock is already in a sustained downtrend: its value declines every day.
When the hammer candle enters the scene, the so-called bulls They think the time has come to get into a buy position - the market is down too low and now is the time to change the share price. The hammer is a visual representation of this mob psychology.
When it comes to exit strategies, there are dozens of options. One way that works well is to stop a stop loss above the flag and wait to see what the market offers you if the trade works well, exit when the momentum slows down.
These technical indicators are, in essence, mathematical functions or equations that are constantly updated in real time on the chart. Ultimately, the value of these indicators is that they could give us an advantage when forecasting future market movements.
Some of these mathematical equations can help you:
Identify if the price of a crypto is trading too high or low
The moving average is a trend summary dominant that tells us what is the degree of consensus between supply and demand.
The MACD is made up of three elements:
The signal line, that detects changes in the momentum of a price and activates buy and sell signals.
