Now that Binance has announced that it is mandatory for all its users to identify themselves, the time has come to get the batteries.
How to verify your identity on Binance has to stop being a mystery. Now what Binance has announced that it is mandatory for all its users to identify themselves, the time has come to put the batteries (regardless of the negative opinions that the news arouses).
3 Step 2: Choose intermediate / identity verification
5 Step 4: fill in the basic identification data
7 Step 6: send one or more photos of your document
9 Step 8: complete the facial verification
Binance requires you to complete all the steps in less than 15 minutes. The exchange also allows up to 10 attempts to verify your identity every 24 hours.
To do this, hover the mouse over the icon "User Center" located at the top right of the navigation bar. Then click on the "Identification" link, as shown here.
Step 2: Choose intermediate / identity verification
Step 3: select nationality or country of residence.
If that is the case, you will not be allowed to transact on the platform. For users in the United States, Binance offers a scaled-down version of its global platform to serve that market called Binance America or Binance.US.
Step 4: fill in the basic identification data
Step 5: choose your identity document
Depending on the document you choose, you will be asked to present one of the two sides of the document. You can only have one photo for the passport, but you will be asked to upload front and back photos for the other two documents.
Binance will use your device's camera to scan your face. You can choose to use your webcam (if you use your computer to verify your identity) or your phone's camera through the Binance app.
The verification exercise typically takes less than an hour, but this process can take up to 36 hours or even longer in peak periods and on rare occasions. Advanced verification (of address)
Binance will ask you to provide a document showing your current address.
On the page, click the "Verify Now" button in the Advanced section. Since you have successfully completed the identity verification stage, this button should be orange and it is clickable.
Only documents issued in the three months prior to the verification date are allowed. The file format to be presented can be PDF, JPEG, JPG, PNG with a file size limited to no more than 5MB.
Although it may seem like a long and tedious process, we promise that getting verified on Binance is simple and hassle-free.
