Today's enigma has come courtesy of an NFT (non-fungible token) that seemed to link to the website of the well-known Banksy, creating a heated debate on social networks: Has Banksy finally released his own NFT work for sale?
This very morning elusive artist Bansky's website promoted the sale of an NFT artwork, which ended up being auctioned this Tuesday. Although the NFT was listed on the artist's website, it is not from Banksy, according to a statement from the artist's authentication body, Pest Control.
Under the title Great Redistribution of the Climate Change Disaster (Great Redistribution of Climate Change Disaster), the Banksy NFT (An 8-bit style image of a figure looking cryptopunk smoking a cigarette in front of four factory smokestacks emitting plumes of smoke) seemed to be a comment on the climate crisis, a topic Banksy has spoken out on in the past. Let's observe how the character is smoking a cigarette that resembles in design the chimneys in the background.
"This is no joke," he told The Art Newspaper. Then, Were you scammed?
It seems that Banksy's market strength is now extending to his hackneyed NFT fans.
