The supports and resistances of a price chart represent key conjunctural moments in which the forces of supply and demand converge. In financial markets, prices are driven by excess supply (down) and excess demand (up).
Demand is synonymous with bullish, bull (bull) and purchase. In slang, an uptrend is known as bullish.
2 What is resistance?
7 Conclusion of supports and resistances
Support is the price level at which demand is considered strong enough to prevent the price from falling further.Logic dictates that as the price falls towards support and becomes cheaper, buyers will be more inclined to buy and sellers will be less inclined to sell.When the price reaches the support level, it is believed that the demand will exceed the supply and prevent the price from falling below the support. In theory, of course.
A break below it indicates that the sellers have beaten the buyers. A decline below support indicates a new willingness to sell and / or a lack of incentive to buy.Once support is broken, another support level will have to be set at a lower level.
Resistance occurs when an uptrend is expected to stop temporarily, due to a concentration of supply.
Support and resistance zones can be identified on the charts by trend lines and moving averages.
Resistance is the price level at which the sell is believed to be strong enough to prevent the price from rising further.Logic dictates that as price moves towards resistance, sellers are more inclined to sell and buyers are less inclined to buy.When the price reaches the resistance level, it is believed that the supply will exceed the demand and prevent the price from rising above the resistance.
In December, the stock returned to support in the mid-30s and formed a low around 33. Finally, in February, the stock returned to support and formed a low around 32½.
Support and resistance: swapping roles Support and resistance share enough common characteristics to be mirror images of each other.Support and resistance are reflected and, in fact, when they are overcome, the roles are exchanged.
A price line that previously functioned as resistance in an uptrend will be considered support.once it has been transferred. The break of the support indicates that the forces of supply have exceeded those of demand.
These ranges tell us that the forces of supply and demand are balanced.When the price breaks the trading range, above or below, it indicates that a winner has emerged and the possible start of a new trend.A break above is a win for the bulls (demand) and a break below is a win for the bears (supply). Before entering a position it is essential to confirm whether the breakout is real or false.
September) more before going down. Enthe following articleYou can read how to apply strategies based on the analysis of support and resistance.
When a support or resistance level is penetrated by an amount
Why use support and resistance zones?
If the trading range spans less than 2 months and the price range is relatively narrow, the most accurate support and resistance levels are best suited. If the trading range spans many months and the price range is relatively large, then it is better to use support and resistance zones.
Identifying key support and resistance levels is an essential ingredient for successful technical analysis. Although it is sometimes difficult to pinpoint support and resistance levels, knowing their existence and location can greatly improve your ability to analyze and forecast.
If a security is approaching a resistance level, it can serve as an alert to look for signs of increased selling pressure and a possible pullback.
