You can send BNB to your MetaMask address even if you haven't added the BSC network to your MetaMask wallet yet, but you will only be able to see the tokens on your wallet from Metamask as soon as you have connected it to the BSC network. If you haven't connected your MetaMask to Binance's smart contract network, you won't be able to see your token balance.
After entering your address and choosing the BSC network, you can enter the amount of the token you want to withdraw and complete the transaction. You also need to transfer some BNB to your address to pay the transaction fees on the BSC network.
After choosing the tokens and entering the amount, you must approve the token you want to exchange, which will allow the smart contract to spend your token.
Transaction fees will vary depending on the network you use. Don't expect to pay exactly $ 0,15 each time you buy a token.
After clicking the swap button, check the fees again and then click the confirm swap button.
