We explain how it works, who is behind the boom in football player NFT trading cards, and how to play Sorare.
If his transfer to PSG is finally confirmed, everything indicates that this will be the case.
1 What is Sorare and how does it work?
2 What teams are available in Sorare
4 Does Sorare have a token?
Some of the rarer cards have fetched considerable sums in the past, but the sale of Ronaldo breaks the record as the most expensive sports NFT. It has also become the most expensive commercial soccer card in history, topping a recent sale of $ 124.230 for a physical card of Erling Haland.
Sorare has recruited many of the world's top soccer clubs in recent months to reach the current number of 154 officially licensed teams. The most recent addition was the Austrian Bundesliga.
Sorare is valued at nearly $ 4.000 billion after its latest round of funding, which took place in July and was run by venture capital firm Benchmark. We're talking about 20 times the value of your current estimated earnings, not far behind the multiple of Facebook Inc.'s earnings when it went public.
Example of equipment that can be formed in Sorare.
Why is Sorare so valuable? As we read in an article in the specialized medium Bloomberg, the phenomenon of NFTs responds to a certain «post-pandemic rush to spend money on virtual goods, combined with the psychological hooks of gaming trading and the promise of life-changing riches through cryptocurrencies. '
Investors backing these NFT games praise its clean and lucrative business model, driven by huge profits from cryptocurrency trading. A game like Sorare has an instantly understandable consumer "wrapper" around its crypto core; it is a mix of fantasy football and the Este or Panini sticker packs that the children of the 90s exchanged in the schoolyard.
There are two possible obstacles ahead for Sorare.
