The behavior of the cryptocurrency market is very emotional. People tend to be greedy when the market is going up, which results in FOMO (fear of missing something).
Conversely, when investors are too greedy, that means the market is about to undergo a correction. This indicator takes into account variables such as the volatility of Bitcoin, its dominance, trends, activity in social networks, the momentum and market volume.
This means that in most cases we will want to be in Bitcoin (or cash) when Bitcoin's dominance is in an uptrend, and then we will be more interested in being in alts (including ETH, large caps, mid caps, low caps, etc) when Bitcoin's dominance is in a downtrend.
