Why does the BCH have a better view of the market than its counterpart?
The BTC boom has been on the rise since its market launch. However, after almost a decade, the network responsible for this cryptocurrency have experienced a variety of complications:
As a general rule, it takes several hours before an operation is confirmed by validators on the network. This is because the number capable of validating per second is estimated at 5-8.
Lags and lag in performance are due to design. Blocks on the BTC network have a maximum size of 1 MB.
On the other hand, there are the BCH supporters, whose ideal lies in the fact that the activity on the blockchain develop naturally.
Notably, prior to Bitcoin Cash, the community had already failed to increase the maximum block size. The most significant currencies and that, despite they were not successful projects, were close to achieving it, were:
At this point, it is important to note that the channels of both cryptocurrencies they were united before the first of August.
Contrary to Bitcoin, BCH has a better answer deal with complex situations. This translates into greater stability and profitability in the short term.
And thanks to the fact that the original size of the BTC did not exceed one megabyte, the SegWit2x protocol increased it to 2 MB.
This allowed them to reach a maximum size of 8 MB in mid-2017. As an effect of this expansion, transactions became fast and efficient.
Because Bitcoin Cash maintains a different hash algorithm to that of the BTC network, the repetition between both chains is no longer possible. And in the event that BCH splits in the future, there is a protection plan in place that will make it easier to counter possible repeats.
