Players will find everything they expect from an immersive MMORPG, including free-form sandbox gameplay, a world rich in story, Classless combat, PvP and PvE, a player-driven economy, marketable cosmetics, an artist workshop for community-generated NFTs, an impressive character skill progression, and an AI manager that directs the game to enhance the player experience.
Ember Sword brings together artists, players and builders to create a vast and persistent MMORPG universe in which the community takes ownership and He continually decides the fate of the world and the experiences that are lived in it.
Whether you are a peaceful gatherer of goods or a fierce warrior without mercy, in Ember Sword there will be a place for you: a place where peace and war are chosen by the players themselves. A place built by the player.
Ember Sword is more than a game, it is a community, a world, an economy. It is a living, breathing world in which the owners build and evolve the universe and monetize their own parcels, in which players are free to do what they want when they want.
-Lessons: None. Take part in combat as you see fit.
-Persistent sandbox: Evolve the game world over time with other players.
-Join the team: Make your mark on the game by designing and submitting character models, skins, and emotes.
-Real estate agent: Purchase valuable land and dynamically alter an adventurer's experience by placing resources, monsters, and NPCs, as well as creating unique services and experiences.
Regular Parcels are the basic form of terrain in the game, your chance to own a piece of Thanabus. Regular plots come with the title of Lord / Lady and have traits that are revealed as the game world unfolds, which can include camps, NPC houses, resource depots, monster spawns, and much more.
They can be large resupply stations, guild outposts, and much more. Settlements come with the title of Baron / Baroness and examples of what you can build include small player dwellings, small guild houses, and small player shops.
They house buildings intended for more specific tasks, such as crafting, acquiring specific equipment, and refining resources. A city grants you the title of count And, in addition to all the buildings in the settlement, you can build refinement stations, crafting buildings, medium guild houses, and a bag, a structure that gives you access to the global item trading network.
The largest structures and guilds are found in these urban locations, which brings endless opportunities. The owners of cities are given the title of duke or Duchess and, in addition to all the buildings in the settlements and towns, the cities allow you to build great guild houses, portals, caravan trading posts, and much more!
