6 How to choose the best planet to mine
CryptoMines is a science fiction NFT game designed to provide users with a fun experience by collecting workers and spaceships to travel through the universe in search of $ ETERNAL, this mineral allows them to live another day and get some benefits in the road.
CryptoMines aims to be the biggest sci-fi game on the blockchain, allowing its users to enjoy being part of a vast universe, the thrill of strategic play and, of course, winning $ ETERNAL.
The assets are NFTs owned by the players, minted in the ERC-721 standard, which can be traded on our market or sold via P2P to another player.
To start playing CryptoMines, the easiest thing is to go to their page official website, link your Metamask wallet and buy some tokens to get your first team of miners. How to mine planets
The rarity of your workers determines your Mining Power, which in turn defines which planets you can go to. So if, for example, you have two rarity 2 workers and a rarity 2 spaceship, you can go to a Lv2 planet with 200 MP.
The rewards awarded for planet resources are fixed depending on the planet. There is an oracle to maintain the dollar value of the rewards system and prevent them from quickly depleting.
The spaceships will allow our workers to be transported to new planets where they will obtain better rewards based on the Mining Power acquired.
Once we have minted the workers for our crew, these will have big differences depending on their rarity, find the best workers, and increase your profits to new galaxies!
1 star workers are burned for 20% of their cost in $ ETERNAL and will not charge the player back even if they are hired.
Each worker can be hired for a minimum of 7 days, but you can also hire him for 15 or even 30 days, once his contract expires, you will have to hire him again if you want him to continue being part of your Guild. If you wish to fire a worker and they have an active contract, they will be charged an additional amount for the cancellation of their contract (this dismissal rate will not apply if it is a 1-star worker).
How to choose the best planet to mine
Currently there are 30 planets known to the federation, our Workers travel to and from these planets depending on the size of the fleet and the mining power contributed by the Workers.
In our latest update, guilds with sufficient Mining Power will be labeled Veterans, these guilds have a better chance of conducting a successful exploration on less dangerous planets.
Guilds will have better chances when facing trouble on less dangerous planets, this increases your success rate by 2% per planet when traveling to a lower level planet and will stack as long as you have a maximum success rate of 88% . As an example, let's say you have 2.000 Mine Power that allows you to travel to the 20th Planet.
