Solana developers want to exemplify that, by carrying out a different algorithm variation, this is reduced and the network is saturated. Therefore, they hope to achieve higher performance coupled with higher trading volume.
Solana Labs was born in the 2017s under the leadership of Anatoly Yakovenko. The purpose of this organization is to carry out a new transaction verification system, better known as Proof-of-History (PoH).
SOL uses the SPL protocol - a network blockchain token standard. Which facilitates the creation of new tokens for developers without the need to start over.
One of the most interesting aspects of SOL is that it burns in a deflationary process integrated. Not to mention that cryptocurrency holders can become validators of the network.
In addition, nowadays new DApps are being designed using this network as the epicenter. Reason why, the use of SOL is expanding impressively.
On the other hand, regular and Solana blockchains differ in their ability to parallelize transactions. This model is known as Sealevel: a technology that streamlines the execution of smart contracts in parallel.
This system stands out because it is capable of generating a vast chain of events without interruptions. Consequently, it generates a simple, verifiable chain of operations, which is then added to a block by a validator.
The SOL cryptocurrency is accompanied by a block propagation protocol that encourages the correct distribution of nodes and information.
This protocol split the block information in small sections that are distributed through the network. Afterwards, the fragments are joined by the nodes according to the individual states of each one.
In a simple and fast way, the nodes of the Solana network are capable of accessing the data responsible for the recreation of the blocks. In fact, the same network designs the blocks through an election based on a quorum.
Rather, they have an essential role in the selection of the next group of validator nodes.
If this is not confirmed in less than half a second, the system proceeds to make an output: the failure of the operation. Consequently, it informs the user that they must perform the operation again.
For this reason it is estimated that the SOL token was developed to compete against Ethereum. Especially when it comes to DeFi and DApps support.
This gives them a clear advantage over their main competitors, since EOS and Ethereum can only work on one action at a time.
On the other hand, Solana's smart contracts are based on the C and Rust language, in order to design a more sophisticated ecosystem.
Tower BFT has the role of judge within the system of timestamps (timetamps) that are executed in Solana. It uses a synchronized clock between the nodes, which serve as a point of control, verification and acceptance.
This is the reason that the network has shorter generation times than the average blockchain. A job made possible by PoH technology in company with Tower BFT.
That is the number one reason why people prefer the SOL coin, it is backed by:
Your ability to generate blocks in half a second. While its main competitors, Bitcoin and Ethereum, last between 10 minutes or 20 seconds, as far as it is concerned.
