Account of one of the administrators of the Telegram group, where he has hair and signs how he lived the non-development of the game.
As we already warned from Café con CriptosThis NFT game (which started out as a shitcoin) will never see the light of day. Below we show you a transcript (suitably corrected) of the story of one of the administrators of the Telegram group, where he has hair and signs how he lived the non-development of the game.
Everything was going well, we talked almost daily with the devs, the graphics kept going up, the publicity started with the youtubers, a lot of people began to enter the group and ask a lot of questions (obviously) about the project. Some questions we knew how to answer because we had the information, but for others we didn't know what to answer because we (the mods) didn't have the information either, since the devs hardly told us anything.
The date of the sales of the NFTs came, and it started to get messy, since people did not like that the sale was in BNB instead of pipemoon tokens. I would start talking to Irving and tell him that I didn't like the attitude of the devs, and that I was afraid this would end up being scam in the end.
In general, the mods were super stressed, the graph was going down, thousands of messages in the group, hundreds of messages to our private ... and the devs did not give us information. Above, the date of the game, the famous September 13, was already close.
When I was about to leave, Abelardo arrived and told Irving that he would show him photos of the game later. We waited for later and he did indeed send Irving a picture of the game.
Well, he stayed in the mod, they expelled me and all the blame went to me. The mods that they continued to defend just continued to get people excited.
In their consciences, they know it.
