Step 1: Log into your account and navigate to the page.
The page has three sections: Basic, intermediate and advanced verification. Let's go through the last two verifications, as the basic level verification will have been completed by default when you create your account.
You have to complete the intermediate / identity verification before proceeding to the advanced verification. Click the Verify button to continue with the identity verification.
In this step, you will be provided with a dialog box that will ask you to select your country of residence. This information is important because Binance must comply with various regulations specific to each location., and their systems and policies may not be followed in your region.
There are two stages to identity verification, as outlined on this page. In the first stage, you will present your basic information, and in the next stage, you will provide identity documents and face verification.
Next, you will need to select from three available government-issued identity document options. You can have more than one of these documents, but Binance only requires one of them.
