MIR4 is one of the first real games to use a "play-to-earn" gameplay model in an MMORPG, which is really getting a lot of young players excited.
6 How to get and mine Dark Steel in MIR4
As with any other MMORPG game, one of the main advantages of playing this game is having or being a member of a clan. Other than that, MIR4 has its own story and the setting is very realistic, giving players the option to explore the map, allowing the game to have more flexibility than other MMORPGs.
99% of readers will agree that to attract a player to a game, it must have neat and impressive graphics. In this respect, MIR4 is an NFT game that stands out above the rest, be it Cryptoblades or even Wanaka Farm.
After downloading your application, you can create an account simply using your Gmail or linking your Facebook account.
You can choose from the following four classes:
Sorcerer - A wizard who uses the power of the elements to defeat his enemies. Although he was formidable when fighting alone, he was even more so when surrounded by comrades.
Lancer - A battlefield tyrant who uses his long spear to oppress his adversary. Destroy the opponent's formation and eliminate the target at all costs, equipped with simultaneous attack and protection moves.
A staple in every MMORPG is doing or finishing certain tasks / missions that will give you a lot of boost in your early days as a MIR4 player.
MIR4 will give you 30 tasks that you can finish daily. These provide experience points and other useful resources that you can use to enchant equipment.
MMORPG games wouldn't be exciting if there wasn't a clan involved. MIR4's clan structure is very well designed, since at some point you will need your clan members for certain tasks and you can ask them to follow you in your search and finish it with their help.
Additionally, clan leaders can set the required power level before a certain player can join the clan. Knowing how to level up in MIR4 is essential, because there will be areas where, if you don't have enough level, you will be quickly annihilated.
How to get and mine Dark Steel in MIR4
MIR4 has many valleys or locations where players can mine Darksteel, an essential resource that is used to exchange for DRACO tokens or to upgrade your equipment and make yourself stronger.
In addition, the MIR4 clans also have other functionalities such as assassination, diplomacy, and resource policy, so make sure you never play alone.
The DRACO is the main reason for the exponential growth of MIR4, since players not only want to play, but also monetize their time by playing certain games.
Players can get DRACO by trading Darksteel, an essential resource that can be mined in the game.
The model was created with the purpose of protecting the token against the decline in real value caused by in-game inflation and did so by limiting its daily and total casting volume, and provides medium and long-term investment opportunities for the game.
