However, this quality will have its negative aspect: good in everything, expert in nothing. In the brief gameplay that we have seen, we see the ability to perform melee hits and a spell with channeling to attack the enemy from a distance.
Enchanters correspond to the archetype of magicians / sorcerers (not to be confused with witches): characters focused on casting spells, with little physical capacity and preferably played from a distance.
Rangers correspond to the ranger archetype: a mixture of ranged and melee damage, with support skills and accompanied by an animal companion. So far, it has been the only class to show a "pet" that accompanies the player, and the functionality that this element will bring to the class remains to be specified.
All Witch hunters correspond to the rogue archetype: damage capacity through both ranged and melee weapons, and damage abilities but mainly crowd control. At the statistical level, They will have less durability than the rest of the classes that can fight melee, but like the Enchanters, they will have a much higher damage capacity since it will be a class focused on DPS.
