It is not easy to know how to identify a scam in an NFT game. In this guide to identify SCAMS in NFT games we give you the 10 essential keys when evaluating the quality of a project.
How to detect NFT scam games is becoming an increasingly difficult challenge. As we have seen recently with cases such as the failed launch of Block Monsters, know how to detect fraud in new NFT games it is a skill that requires more and more hours of research.
11 Detecting NFT scam games is always up to you
Your design must be clear, clean, consistent and detailed. At a first glance, we should be able to quickly answer fundamental questions such as: What type of product are we investing in?
Distrust NFT games that do not present this type of information in an accessible way for an investor of any level, or also those that have the web page created in a generic way or following a template. This denotes little effort for design care.
Its founding letter. It must specify relevant information for all types of investors: from the fundamental idea, the "history", modes, or functionalities of the game ... to the economic aspect or tokenomics of the game token: systems of the internal economy, budget distribution, marketing actions, specifications and functions of the token and the NFTs, or short, medium and long term plans among others.
The quality of the writing is another critical factor: a whitepaper with misspellings or “empty” paragraphs of text of content makes an intolerable lack of professionalism appear. If you want to see an example of goodwhitepaper, take a look at the one of Star atlas through this link.
The Star Atlas whitepaper is an example of a professional document packed with information.
In case the team is confident in their own work, they should have no problem making their identity public. Having references to previous work or their contacts to social networks (Twitter and / or LinkedIn) to be able to communicate with them gives an extra credibility to the NFT game in question.
Under no circumstances should we go to sources other than the official ones to copy the address of the contract. A very common scam is to meet falsely friendly users who, either in Telegram or Discord, provide us with false contract addresses that only seek to empty uswallet.
It is important to see how the market cap from the launch of the token to its current state. Has it gone up or down?
Once these elements have been identified, it will be time to carry out a study on the events carried out in the project and in its economy. This must be information that we know how to interpret in order to be able to make sure of a possible scam.
What is the percentage of large investors among holders?
Once a share of the investment has been acquired either in the form of tokens or NFTs, we have to know how we can handle them (sell, buy and store them). The ability to participate in tests so that our NFT acquires a greater value, get more tokens, exchange them for other goods ... in short: possibilities and consequences of managing ourselves in the project environment with our investment.
It often happens that many teams promise certain aspects regarding the functionalities that are not fulfilled or do not proceed with the correct use of these. Clear examples are the common appearances of new tokens with the project in an advanced stage of development or the changes and limitations of the project against the promises of its exit.
Under the heading of communication and public relations we collect all the aspects related to the information that the development team releases to its investors and interested parties through the different channels that exist. Wholesome and healthy communication is essential.
Discord: another medium similar to Telegram but with greater capabilities. It is often used as a news repository, an announcement channel, discussion and opinion forums, and even for live Q&A with the development team.
