Users mainland China users will have their accounts switched to "withdrawal mode only"
Binance, theexchange The most famous cryptocurrency exchange (and controversial according to the news that is starring in 2021), is drastically limiting the possibility of trading between pairs of the yuan in response to the blanket ban on all cryptocurrency transactions imposed by China on September 24. Additionally, mainland Chinese users will have their accounts switched to "withdrawal mode only"
Despite being of Chinese origin, Binance seems not to be willing to tolerate the presence of the Chinese currency in the Asian country. In response to the latest regulatory requirements from China, Binance is phasing out the yuan from its consumer-to-consumer (C2C) platform.
Seven days to close Binance account in China
"If the platform finds users in mainland China, their corresponding accounts will be switched to 'withdrawal only' mode, and users will only be able to withdraw, cancel orders, redeem and close positions."
Although Binance had pulled out of the mainland Chinese market in 2017, The firm launched a peer-to-peer platform in 2019 that allowed users to trade cryptocurrencies against the Chinese yuan. Now, in response to China's Sept. 24 blanket ban on cryptocurrency trading, Binance is closing all ties with the Chinese mainland market.
However, with the policy update on September 24, the People's Bank of China (PBOC) took a no-holds-barred approach, banning everything from mining, the operation of cryptocurrency exchanges to the promotion or dissemination of information related to cryptocurrency trading (even closing cryptocurrency-related companies).
Also on Wednesday, OKEX, another major cryptocurrency exchange with origin in China, has expressed in a statement that it has switched its main business to international markets since 2017, and that it stops promoting and providing services to the mainland China market. In its latest move, China added cryptocurrency mining to a preliminary list of industries in which investment is restricted or prohibited.
When demand goes up, prices go up, and when supply goes up, prices go down. When supply and demand are equal, prices move sideways as bulls and bears fight for control.
1 What is technical analysis support?
4 Learning to read supports and resistances
6 Why use support and resistance zones?
What is technical analysis support?
Support levels are typically below the current price, but it is not uncommon for a security to trade at or near support. Since technical analysis is not an exact science, establishing precise support levels can often be difficult.
Support occurs when a downtrend is expected to stop due to a concentration in demand.
Market psychology plays an important role as traders and investors look back on the past and react to changing conditions to anticipate future market movement.
Resistance levels are usually above the current price, but it is not uncommon for a security to trade at or near resistance. Also, price movements can be volatile and rise above resistance briefly.
Supports must be established with the previous reaction minima, while the strengths must be established using the previous reaction maxima. In the following graph we can see the evolution of a lateral trend that was clearly battling between a price range for several months:
If we start to measure from the new trend, which started in October, the support was established with the low of that month, around 31 dollars.
Observe, in the previous graph of PeopleSoft (PSFT), the behavior of supports and resistances with the passage of time.
meaningful, they change their roles and it transforms into the opposite.
If a security is approaching a significant support level, it can serve as an alert to be more attentive to signs of increased buying pressure and a possible change in trend.
In case a support or resistance level is broken, it indicates that the relationship between supply and demand has changed. The break of a resistance indicates that the bulls (the demand) have won the game and the break of a support indicates that the bears (the offer) have won the battle.
