These ships when minted will obtain a rarity level that will define the number of workers that we can transport on our expeditions. Each player will have a maximum limit of 10 ships in their fleet.
Workers are our main mining force and will be deployed to mine $ ETERNAL through the Metaverse, each worker will also have to be kept in the Guild through the use of Contracts.
Workers can be fired (burned) which will return 20% of the minting cost to the player paid in $ ETERNAL, if your worker has been hired, you will have to pay severance to be able to fire him.
Contracts are necessary so that your workers can assist in your expeditions, you can have more workers available in your inventory, however, if they are not currently hired, they will not count towards your total Mining Power.
The Workers travel the galaxy looking for $ ETERNAL and facing serious dangers to extract them, the planets are evaluated depending on the difficulty to extract this precious mineral that gives life, the most dangerous planets are those with the greatest amount of $ ETERNAL in them , thus rewarding the daring adventurers who dare to explore them.
To protect our workforce, the Federation allows them to travel only to the planets they can assume, that is, if we have a fleet made up of Workers with a total amount of Mining Power of 500 we could go to the Fifth planet. Each planet's bounty scales exponentially as one travels further into the Metaverse.
Veteran guilds will get a success bonus for reaching the 1.500 mining power threshold when they return to lower planets. This encourages players to grow their guild, hire more workers, and get more spaceships, not only for more $ ETERNAL but also better success rates.
