IP Rating Checker Want to know what the IP rating on your product means? Use this checker and it will display the level of protection.
A product with an IP00 rating is not protected against solid objects and is not protected against liquids.
2- Protection assured against solid objects that are over 12.5mm (e.g. fingers).
4- Protection assured against solid objects that are over 1mm (e.g.
5- Protected against quantity of dust that could interfere with the normal operation of the product but not fully dust tight. Complete protection against solid objects.
0- No protection assured.
2- Protection assured against vertical drops of water when the product is tilted up to 15° from its normal position.
4- Protection assured against water splashing from any angle.
6- Protection assured against powerful water jets projected by a nozzle (12.5mm) from any angle.
8- Protection assured against long periods of water immersion at a depth of over 1 meter.
Meanings Of Some Common IP Ratings
IP54 —— A product with an IP54 rating is protected against dust ingress sufficient to prevent the product from operating normally but it’s not dust tight. The product is fully protected against solid objects and splashing of water from any angle.
IP65—— If you see IP65 written on a product, this means it is fully dust tight and protected against solid objects. Plus it is protected against water jets projected by a nozzle (6.3mm) from any angle.
IPX4—— An IPX4 rated product is protected from water splashes from any angle.
